{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1276041-what-do-you-think-of-the-chilling-adventures-of-sabrina","id":1276041,"title":"What do you think of The Chilling Adventures of Sabrina?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-22T07:06:59-08:00","id":1276041,"title":"What do you think of The Chilling Adventures of Sabrina?","content":"What the title says.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-22T08:43:43-08:00","id":1276057,"title":"","content":"Granted I've not seen the series, I've only heard about it. That said, I'm not certain it works in MtA terms; it's tone is too light for an actual Nephandus campaign, and the magic used is too easily coincidental for the way magic works in the game, and the setting is not ugly enough for the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-22T13:50:09-08:00","id":1276117,"title":"","content":"The more I've thought about it and the more I'd say that the Church of Night isn't Nephandi but they are infernal, sort of like the Wu Keng they had the power inside all along(see Sabrina) and have made a shitty deal with a terrible Umbrood spirit to survive a horrific period of repression by other groups and now their descendents are toys for said umbrood who may not be Nephandically infernal but is a complete abusive asshole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-22T20:55:50-08:00","id":1276174,"title":"","content":"^^ I'm in agreement with Lian. The Church of Night are an infernalist Craft with some Hemetic and Verbena sensibilities when it comes to their magic. While the show is mostly a dark comedy with some sincere dramatic moments, I think it could work fit in fine in Mage: The Ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-23T07:53:58-08:00","id":1276243,"title":"","content":"While they certainly despise mortals, they're not exactly out to destroy the world and corrupt it into glourious decadence. But they're close enough to make the association.<br /> <br /> They fit in neatly into hermetics (verbena no so much because of the essence of their pacts), or maaaybe hollowers. Great chances of being considered a left-handed group too.<br /> It's certainly a set of good examples of faith, pactualism, ritualism and chaos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 12-24-2018, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T09:03:53-08:00","id":1276809,"title":"","content":"I will repost what I posted on the first thread for this show.<br /> <br /> &quot;It depicts all Witches by equating their religion and practices to Satanism and WICCAN is just an acronym for a feminist power group. Being that my WICCAN friends who if you did not know are also known as witches struggle each day to try to get rid of these blatant stereotypes. Also if you didn't know its stereo types like this that spur hatred towards their religion. Funny story I was once hit in the head with a bible because I was Wiccan, I do prefer it to when I got stabbed because &quot;thou shall not suffer a witch to live&quot; or to the lesser extent when some of my children could not wear their pentacles because the school decided that just those items not crosses or red bandanas were gang signs and the school had a policy against wearing gang signs or the time my mother cried out &quot;your a witch!&quot; when I tried to tell her about my religion in a restaurant and then ran from me like I was Satan himself. Some of the patrons of the restaurant were religious and this is what led to me getting beaten in a ally latter that night.<br /> <br /> That being said I think it is alright for a work of fiction but remember it is just that and not an actual depiction of Witches or Wiccans or there real world struggle nor is it an excuse to cause real world hate.&quot;<br /> <br /> As I said at the end of that post I don't mind discussion as it is a fictional world, but please remember their are people who suffer religious persecution in this country because of misconception garnered from fictional works such as this.<br /> <br /> that being said if you where to use this as a bases for a campaign I personally would just keep it as a fictional work that cause strife in the characters lives or as an attempt by the technocracy to leverage media against their enemies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T10:41:46-08:00","id":1276823,"title":"","content":"I just realized that the 'chilling' part of the series' title is meant to indicate scariness and horror. I thought it was a reference to cold, because I associated &quot;<i>Sabrina the Teenage Witch</i>&quot; ( I never watched or read anything involving Sabrina the Witch ) with an upbeat and cheerful tone and mood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T17:30:21-08:00","id":1276903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1276041-what-do-you-think-of-the-chilling-adventures-of-sabrina?p=1276809#post1276809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will repost what I posted on the first thread for this show.<br /> <br /> &quot;It depicts all Witches by equating their religion and practices to Satanism and WICCAN is just an acronym for a feminist power group. Being that my WICCAN friends who if you did not know are also known as witches struggle each day to try to get rid of these blatant stereotypes. Also if you didn't know its stereo types like this that spur hatred towards their religion. Funny story I was once hit in the head with a bible because I was Wiccan, I do prefer it to when I got stabbed because &quot;thou shall not suffer a witch to live&quot; or to the lesser extent when some of my children could not wear their pentacles because the school decided that just those items not crosses or red bandanas were gang signs and the school had a policy against wearing gang signs or the time my mother cried out &quot;your a witch!&quot; when I tried to tell her about my religion in a restaurant and then ran from me like I was Satan himself. Some of the patrons of the restaurant were religious and this is what led to me getting beaten in a ally latter that night.<br /> <br /> That being said I think it is alright for a work of fiction but remember it is just that and not an actual depiction of Witches or Wiccans or there real world struggle nor is it an excuse to cause real world hate.&quot;<br /> <br /> As I said at the end of that post I don't mind discussion as it is a fictional world, but please remember their are people who suffer religious persecution in this country because of misconception garnered from fictional works such as this.<br /> <br /> that being said if you where to use this as a bases for a campaign I personally would just keep it as a fictional work that cause strife in the characters lives or as an attempt by the technocracy to leverage media against their enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are a lot of groups that are based purely on fiction that do exist in WOD(... see about all of Vampire, or the Doctor showing up in a werewolf book) the witches seem like a pretty good small Hedge magic &quot;cult&quot; it even justifies their unwillingness to go spread out and leave the damned town.<br /> <br /> One could even argue Sabrina is the only one who shows actual Dyanamic magic in the setting(as did her father) thus why the spirit cares so much more for obtaining her Awakened soul than their pathetic shells.<br /> <br /> But from a Mage setting perspective I'd say Greendale is the sort of place your Cabal comes into and kicks over. They fight Hedges mages, demons, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-27T09:04:25-08:00","id":1277014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1276041-what-do-you-think-of-the-chilling-adventures-of-sabrina?p=1276903#post1276903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There are a lot of groups that are based purely on fiction that do exist in WOD(... see about all of Vampire, or the Doctor showing up in a werewolf book) the witches seem like a pretty good small Hedge magic &quot;cult&quot; it even justifies their unwillingness to go spread out and leave the damned town..</div> </div> </div> </div>Please let me be wrong on this and I will assume that I am at this point. But it seemed like you were saying that WICCA is a &quot;cult&quot; that is based purely on fiction?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-27T09:11:04-08:00","id":1277015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1276041-what-do-you-think-of-the-chilling-adventures-of-sabrina?p=1276903#post1276903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...)<br /> But from a Mage setting perspective I'd say Greendale is the sort of place your Cabal comes into and kicks over. They fight Hedges mages, demons, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Amalgam. I really wish someone would do a World of Darkness TV series with Technocrats as protagonists. The visuals and the music could be amazing. The Conventions would provide a lot of variety while maintaining a clear theme, focus, and mood of the show.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T06:56:48-08:00","id":1277350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1276041-what-do-you-think-of-the-chilling-adventures-of-sabrina?p=1277015#post1277015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or Amalgam. I really wish someone would do a World of Darkness TV series with Technocrats as protagonists. The visuals and the music could be amazing. The Conventions would provide a lot of variety while maintaining a clear theme, focus, and mood of the show.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's agents of shield...men in black...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T06:58:17-08:00","id":1277351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1276041-what-do-you-think-of-the-chilling-adventures-of-sabrina?p=1277014#post1277014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please let me be wrong on this and I will assume that I am at this point. But it seemed like you were saying that WICCA is a &quot;cult&quot; that is based purely on fiction?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Dude, he literally mentioned the show's specific group right after that phrase. Chill. Second hand offendedness is not really conducive to getting this thread anywhere. It makes agreeing with your comment on how the story's group is not representative of anything else unnecessarily hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 12-29-2018, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T07:12:10-08:00","id":1277356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1276041-what-do-you-think-of-the-chilling-adventures-of-sabrina?p=1277015#post1277015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or Amalgam. I really wish someone would do a World of Darkness TV series with Technocrats as protagonists. The visuals and the music could be amazing. The Conventions would provide a lot of variety while maintaining a clear theme, focus, and mood of the show.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a really good idea. It could be about a pair of FBI agents who work to uncover a shadow government and their nefarious schemes that include secret eugenics programs and biological warfare, super soldiers and androids, and hiding the existence of and resisting life beyond Earth with <i>even worse</i> plans for humanity than the shadow government itself. Throw in monsters of the week to show how gritty and awful the world really is, and how that shadow government works through the public government and media to hide the supernatural from the masses, to keep the show fresh and the audience guessing what waits around the corner. One of the agents could be a nutso conspiracy theorist, and the other a hardcore empiricist and skeptic, to get some conflict and chemistry in its core cast.<br /> <br /> So, snark aside, I like Sabrina. Yeah, its closest parallel in WoD would be a cabal of hedge mages left in the cold, struggling against ancient infernal pacts made for survival. They're definitely closer in nature with Verbena, or <i>maybe</i> a left-handed Chorister path, than Hermetics in my opinion. All the sex, cannibalism, and focus on blood and ritual sacrifice are the clinchers for me. <i>Maybe</i> a really left-handed Chorister path, since they're theistic Satanists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 12-29-2018, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T07:22:58-08:00","id":1277358,"title":"","content":"The big point against verbena is who and how they bonded with the divine. You can still feel the animism off their magics, but the very specific deal with the devil feels very off.<br /> Well, there's a reason hermetics and verbena are so close that the friction's palpable.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T07:34:25-08:00","id":1277359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1276041-what-do-you-think-of-the-chilling-adventures-of-sabrina?p=1277356#post1277356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's actually a really good idea. It could be about a pair of FBI agents who work to uncover a shadow government and their nefarious schemes that include secret eugenics programs and biological warfare, super soldiers and androids, and hiding the existence of and resisting life beyond Earth with <i>even worse</i> plans for humanity than the shadow government itself. Throw in monsters of the week to show how gritty and awful the world really is, and how that shadow government works through the public government and media to hide the supernatural from the masses, to keep the show fresh and the audience guessing what waits around the corner. One of the agents could be a nutso conspiracy theorist, and the other a hardcore empiricist and skeptic, to get some conflict and chemistry in its core cast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ever since I read about the Technocracy in M:tA, all the other conspiracies and secret governments ( from comic books, TV series, or books ) seem miserable and unfocused in comparison. One of the primary reasons is that the persons running these conspiracies are often replacable ( and in fact, it is a very common storyline element for them to get replaced ) because individuals don't have much going for themselves once they become outplayed or exposed. While Technocrats are Mages, so their capabilities and comprehension are above and beyond what mundane humans are capable ; and individuals can have considerably specialized or unique capabilities. This solidifies Technocracy as an influential and powerful conspiracy in a way that I haven't seen in any other fictions.<br /> Also in fictions there is often division between those who are scientists and technology experts, and those who are in leadership or organizational roles. A Technocrat can act in regard to science and research, and leadership and organization, at the same time. This is another trait of Technocracy that makes them very distinct and interesting in comparison to other conspiracies and organizations in fictions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1276041-what-do-you-think-of-the-chilling-adventures-of-sabrina?p=1277356#post1277356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, snark aside, I like Sabrina. Yeah, its closest parallel in WoD would be a cabal of hedge mages left in the cold, struggling against ancient infernal pacts made for survival. They're definitely closer in nature with Verbena, or <i>maybe</i> a left-handed Chorister path, than Hermetics in my opinion. All the sex, cannibalism, and focus on blood and ritual sacrifice are the clinchers for me. <i>Maybe</i> a really left-handed Chorister path, since they're theistic Satanists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't thought about the possibility of 'Left-handed Choristers' before. It is not as interesting or distinct as Nephandi who are Chorister Barrabis, but it is definitely intriguing to think about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-29-2018, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T07:38:15-08:00","id":1277361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1276041-what-do-you-think-of-the-chilling-adventures-of-sabrina?p=1277358#post1277358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big point against verbena is who and how they bonded with the divine. You can still feel the animism off their magics, but the very specific deal with the devil feels very off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Verbena are perfectly capable of being infernalists as well, Verbena aren't all followers of some form of druidism, and don't forget the Maleficia practice is most common among Verbena. I don't think an argument about House Diedne would really apply either, since Diedne were specifically a druidic House. The witches' religion in Sabrina is theistic Satanism, that seems to be an antithesis of Christianity itself and its assimilation of pagan practices and holidays, as opposed to directly derived from pagan beliefs themselves. Honestly, contemporary Christianity (at least in practice) has more in common with European paganism, by way of cultural assimilation during the religion's spread, than it does with Judaism.<br /> <br /> Which is why I say there'd be a stronger argument for them being left-handed Choristers, than Hermetics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 12-29-2018, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T00:38:52-08:00","id":1277785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1276041-what-do-you-think-of-the-chilling-adventures-of-sabrina?p=1277361#post1277361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...) and don't forget the Maleficia practice is most common among Verbena.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that maleficia might be close to as common ( if not more common ) among the Cult of Ecstasy. There are numerous groups of Ecstatic Mages who could be deemed to be left-handed Mages. The Nine Sacred Passions of this Tradition - Joy/Wonder, Love, Empathy/Sympathy, Lust/Ambition, Grief/Sadness, Fear, Jealousy/Envy, Hate, Rage - include four passions / emotions which could be considered to be negative or unpleasant emotions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 01-01-2019, 03:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T12:55:39-08:00","id":1277900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1276041-what-do-you-think-of-the-chilling-adventures-of-sabrina?p=1277014#post1277014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please let me be wrong on this and I will assume that I am at this point. But it seemed like you were saying that WICCA is a &quot;cult&quot; that is based purely on fiction?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Witches of Sabrina(the Church of Night) is a cult based entirely on fictious ideas. But there are plenty of things that are completely based on IRL fiction without any folkloric belief that exist whole sale in the World of Darkess(its called Vampire the Masquerade)<br /> <br /> Wicca is a real world religion, that they inexpicably try to connect to Sabrina even though it has nothing to do with anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T12:57:50-08:00","id":1277901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1276041-what-do-you-think-of-the-chilling-adventures-of-sabrina?p=1277015#post1277015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or Amalgam. I really wish someone would do a World of Darkness TV series with Technocrats as protagonists. The visuals and the music could be amazing. The Conventions would provide a lot of variety while maintaining a clear theme, focus, and mood of the show.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Not really? I mean &quot;Secret Government organization that fights against the Supernatural&quot; is a pretty damned common TV show concept. I Mean the Twist with the Technocracy is THEY are just another Supernatural abusing organization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T02:45:44-08:00","id":1278021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1276041-what-do-you-think-of-the-chilling-adventures-of-sabrina?p=1277901#post1277901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Not really? I mean &quot;Secret Government organization that fights against the Supernatural&quot; is a pretty damned common TV show concept. I Mean the Twist with the Technocracy is THEY are just another Supernatural abusing organization.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wrote about Technocrats and how they compare to groups in other fictions in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1276041-what-do-you-think-of-the-chilling-adventures-of-sabrina?p=1277359#post1277359\">this</a> post, and I wrote about Technocrats in a TV show in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1277411-what-would-you-want-from-a-wod-show?p=1277681#post1277681\">this</a> post.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy is not a government organization. They have a lot of influence in governments of mundane humans ; but I think this is not that distinctive, considering that other Mages, and other Nightfolk, can also have influence in governments.<br /> The Technocracy's goals are more complex than &quot;fighting against the supernatural&quot; . Under an idealist perspective, subduing of mundane humans' ability to believe in the supernatural is done for the purpose of advancing science more easily, and because mundane humans can't be trusted in regard to knowing about some facts. I think a more practical perspective is the more interesting one here. According to it, the Technocracy covers up the existence of the supernatural, and promotes logic and scientific viewpoints because they think that it is easier to control what happens, and how mundans humans think and act, under such conditions.<br /> I think that a major priority of the Technocracy ( more important than subduing the belief in the supernatural ) - if it can be said to have clearly defined priorities as a faction / organization / group - is advancing Enlightened Science ; so in a way they aren't much different from Mystic Mages.<br /> Also, the Technocrats are willing to cooperate with other supernatural persons, providing some conditions are met.<br /> <br /> I think what makes the Technocracy very distinct and different as a fictional group / organization is that they are Mages. Thus, individuals and smaller groups matter as much - if not more - than the larger organization. The Conventions of Technocracy are very often described as separate groups / factions. Unlike in other fictional conspiracies or groups, the Technocrats are not made capable, powerful, and influential because of the Technocracy enabling that. Rather, separate Mages who are Technocrats, and each of the Conventions, acts and works to make the Technocracy what it is. Also, due to the fact that Technocrats are Mages ( Enlightened ) there is the unique trait and setting element that those individuals are truly qualified and capable compared to mundane humans. Technocrats being Mages means that they have a lot of self-initiative, and variety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 01-02-2019, 05:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}